M159's patch 0039 said this about ANGLE and it is true of Dawn too: a
platform detection that is a list of operating system names has no answer for
an operating system that is not on it, and every file behind it is already
written to need only the generic one.

dawn/src/utils/platform.h checks _WIN32, __linux__, __APPLE__, __Fuchsia__
and __EMSCRIPTEN__ and then stops with #error "Unsupported platform." What
sits behind it does not care which of those it was:

  SystemHandle.h   using Handle = int   under DAWN_PLATFORM_IS(POSIX)
  DynamicLib.cpp   dlopen/dlsym/dlclose under DAWN_PLATFORM_IS(POSIX)
  SystemUtils.cpp  getenv and /proc     under DAWN_PLATFORM_IS(POSIX)

- and each of those three says so in its own words, with
#error "Unsupported platform for DynamicLib" in the arm this reaches. Ten of
the twenty-three failures a -k 0 build of //third_party/blink/public:blink
had were that one missing arm.

__unix__ is the arm. It names no operating system, and on every platform
Dawn ships on it is unreachable, because each is matched by an earlier one.

Dawn is in this build at all because Blink's WebGPU sources include its
headers - not because anything here can use a GPU. use_dawn is false and
dawn/native is not built; what compiles is dawn/common, which is a platform
abstraction and a handful of utilities.

diff --git a/third_party/dawn/src/utils/platform.h b/third_party/dawn/src/utils/platform.h
--- a/third_party/dawn/src/utils/platform.h
+++ b/third_party/dawn/src/utils/platform.h
@@ -95,6 +95,15 @@
 #define DAWN_PLATFORM_IS_POSIX 1
 #include <emscripten/emscripten.h>
 
+#elif defined(__unix__)
+// A POSIX system this list does not name. Everything in dawn/common that
+// branches on a platform branches on DAWN_PLATFORM_IS(POSIX) once the
+// Windows and Fuchsia cases are past - SystemHandle's `using Handle = int`,
+// DynamicLib's dlopen, SystemUtils' getenv and /proc - so the generic arm is
+// all any of them needs, and each of them says so itself with
+// #error "Unsupported platform for DynamicLib" rather than by assuming.
+#define DAWN_PLATFORM_IS_POSIX 1
+
 #else
 #error "Unsupported platform."
 #endif
